    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The suite contains the single `AcceptanceTest`, which now passes along with a successful compile.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` flag \u2014 true when the owner's city already holds 40\u201349 owners (approaching the hard limit of 50), which stays enforced by the unchanged `RejectCrowdedCity`.\n\nChanges, kept deliberately small and cohesive to minimize structural impact:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `capacityWarning` boolean to the `OwnerDto` schema (generates the DTO getter/setter), mirroring `bulkSignupWarning`.\n\n2. **`CityCapacity.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny, self-contained utility with one static `approaching(owner, repository)` method, modeled on the existing `BulkSignup` helper. It counts owners in the city (case-insensitively) and returns true for `40 \u2264 count < 50`.\n\n3. **`RespondWithOwner.java`** \u2014 one added line: `dto.setCapacityWarning(CityCapacity.approaching(owner, ownerRepository));`, right beside the existing warning assignment.\n\nThe new behavior lives entirely in a fresh single-method class (WMC_other \u2248 0), and the only edited method (`RespondWithOwner.service`) stays a trivial linear responder \u2014 so no existing method or class grows in complexity.",
